 Findings are numbered from UX-37, after UX-36, the highest UX ID in `docs/process/`.
+
+## Findings so far (being confirmed; the final table is in section 5)
+
+- **UX-37 (High):** the drawer headline shows one place's range, unlabelled, while the card shows the span:
+  Amazon amazon:10371179, card "$60K–129K · 4 places", drawer "$83K–117K" (Bellevue's row only). 2,201 of
+  2,260 Amazon postings with 2+ place ranges, and all 255 such Microsoft postings.
+- **UX-38 (Medium):** Amazon's "Project/Program/Product Management--Technical" and "--Non-Tech" are cut to
+  the same visible text: "Project/Program/Produ…" in the filter list, "Project/Program/Product Managem…" in
+  the phone chart rows, and the Ranges legend keys.
+- **UX-39 (Medium):** on a phone, Amazon's first-page preview cards are in the collapsed sheet. For about
+  7 s (Fast 4G, 4x CPU) the first screen shows only the chart skeleton and "Loading 22,179 roles…".
+- **UX-40 (Medium):** chart row sub-lines mix two forms in one chart: "1,215 · $178K US" next to
+  "759 roles · median $161K in the US". "US" is not explained.
+- **UX-41 (Medium):** Ranges stacked rows are labelled only "14 roles" (with "×14" at the bar). Microsoft's
+  $166K–296K band is still 9 rows (3, 6, 14, 5, 5, 2, 2, 2, 2 roles), split by colour and stripe.
+- **UX-42 (Low):** circle counts overflow their circles: Microsoft "118" (22.2 px text in a 21.5 px
+  circle), NVIDIA "115" and "191". A smaller circle has a count while a bigger neighbour has none.
+- **UX-43 (Low):** for one posting the edge chip is a bare "›" or "‹", which reads as a "next" chevron.
+- **UX-44 (Medium):** the stats line shows only "Details▾" when no role in view has pay (Google, Map, a pin
+  of 18 roles with no pay).
+- **UX-45 (Medium):** Juice cut-offs differ on one board: the list says "Juicy: $95K or more · Ripe:
+  $47K–95K", the map legend "$96K or more · $48K–$96K" (methodology: Ripe $47,103, Juicy $94,996).
+- **UX-46 (Medium):** the drawer percentile line is cut off on a phone: "Pays more than 20% of Google's
+  internships in Ca…", "…NVIDIA's internships in the US" (white-space: nowrap, ellipsis).
+- **UX-47 (Medium):** phone density, "Same role elsewhere": four secondary lines of 12–31 words, 2–4 lines
+  each, above the bars.
+- **UX-48 (Medium):** phone density, the Juice line "…in Irving (using Dallas's rent and living costs, the
+  nearest city with cost data)": 19–24 words, 2–3 lines.
+- **UX-49 (Medium):** phone density, the Insights Pay estimate card: explain 20–30 words / 3–5 lines,
+  accuracy 2 lines, as-of 2 lines, auto 2 lines.
+- **UX-50 (Low):** Google "Company" grouping: the card's dot takes the company's colour but sits next to
+  the department name ("● User Experience and Design" in YouTube orange).
+- Still open from round 2: UX-35 (the Juice explainer: 30 words, 3 lines, 5 facts on every board on a phone),
+  UX-36 (Ranges still reads "Group: None" beside "Colour: department"), UX-25 (map pins "371 jobs"; a pin
+  tip "18 jobs … 18 postings"), UX-28 (one block shows "IC3 $102.1K–202.2K" over "Redmond … $102K–235K").
